# Walkthrough - Multi-Page & Theme Fixes

I have addressed the reported issues where multiple pages were not generating (specifically in 4-Koma mode) and the theme color was not changing.

## Changes

### 1. Multi-Page Generation Fix
The issue was caused by a hardcoded restriction in 4-Koma mode that forced the page count to 1.
- **[src/utils/stateConsistency.js](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/utils/stateConsistency.js)**: Removed the logic that forced `totalPages = 1` when `yonkomaMode` is active.
- **[src/components/settings/CompositionSettings.jsx](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/components/settings/CompositionSettings.jsx)**: Enabled the page count buttons (`+` / `-`) even when in 4-Koma mode.
- **[src/utils/layoutGenerator.js](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/utils/layoutGenerator.js)**: Updated the generator to use the requested `totalPages` instead of defaulting to 1 for 4-Koma.
- **[src/utils/storyExpander.js](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/utils/storyExpander.js)**: Updated the story generation logic to create enough dialogue lines for multiple 4-Koma pages (4 lines per page).

### 2. Theme Color Implementation
The "Theme Color" issue was due to the lack of a feature to map "Manga Style" keywoards to UI colors. I have implemented a system that changes the application's color scheme based on the selected style.
- **[src/App.jsx](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/App.jsx)**: Added logic to inject a `data-theme` attribute into the root element based on `settings.mangaStyle`.
    - **Shoujo/Romance** -> `shoujo` (Pink/Light)
    - **Horror** -> `horror` (Dark Red)
    - **Sci-Fi/Cyberpunk** -> `scifi` (Neon Blue)
    - **Retro/Watercolor** -> `retro` (Sepia)
    - **Others** -> `default` (Dark Gray)
- **[src/App.css](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/App.css)**: Refactored column background colors to use CSS variables (`var(--col-settings-bg)`, etc.) to allow theming.
- **[src/styles/GlobalStyles.css](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/styles/GlobalStyles.css)**: Defined the CSS variables for each theme (Standard, Shoujo, Horror, SciFi, Retro).

## Verification Results

### Multi-Page 4-Koma
- **Scenario**: User selects "4コマ漫画風" and sets pages to 2.
- **Result**:
    - The UI now allows setting 2 pages.
    - `layoutGenerator` calculates `targetPages = 2`.
    - `storyExpander` generates ~8 lines of text.
    - [distributePanels](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/utils/mangaDistribution.js#140-227) loops through 2 pages, creating 2 vertical strips.

### Theme Switching
- **Scenario**: User changes "画風スタイル" to "少女漫画風".
- **Result**:
    - [App.jsx](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/App.jsx) detects "少女漫画風" and sets `data-theme="shoujo"`.
    - [GlobalStyles.css](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/styles/GlobalStyles.css) applies the pink/light color variables.
    - The application background, sidebar, and accents change color immediately.
